  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-04-10T23:32:21.749Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "(Moving from here: https://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/1375-pico-vrchat-problems-bugs )\n\nAs of Build 1435, which just got released on Pico, the avatar hands now appear to be in line with the controllers, however it seems the -controller- offsets are broken instead, in the opposite direction; the in-game render model is too far forward.\n\nIt seems like the avatar hands were moved to be in-line with the in-game render model, but the render model was also moved forward.\n\nAdditionally, I feel like the avatar hands are pitched a little too far up. The fingers should be closer to the handle. If I remember correctly about a 20 degree wrist angle offset prior to this update made it feel right angle-wise.\n\nThey look to be about the same distance as before, see: https://youtube.com/watch?v=TVpc1-cWkOI",
